Subject: [PATCH 365/488] V2 runner sampling: int32 positions draw as Triton's
 do

Triton's tl.randint takes an int32 position as the Philox offset's only word
and adds the draft salt in 32 bits; the TileLang Gumbel sampler and sink
candidates required int64 positions, and the rejection sampler's unbiasedness
test draws its proposals with int32 ones. The positions' dtype is part of both
kernels' keys (int64 in serving, as declared), and the uncached sampler's
placeholder column no longer borrows the positions.
---
